# Build artifacts.
#
# Binaries go to bin/ and are never written to the repository root: the root
# already has a vyql/ directory (the runtime data), so a root-level `vyql` entry
# here would match that directory and silently drop the entire knowledge base.
#
# The same name collision has a second edge. `go build -o vyql` from the root
# does not fail -- vyql/ is a directory, so Go writes the binary INSIDE it, as
# vyql/vyql. That is a 70 MB artifact sitting in the middle of the data tree.
/vyql/vyql
/bin/
*.test
*.out

# Go
vendor/

# Node (script tooling)
node_modules/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Agent session data
.claude/

# Secrets
*.env
*.pem
*.key
